    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d512">

                <pb facs="0763" n="649" xml:id="pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4A6/174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-12T13:00:00+00:00">November 12, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 12—10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>293. From Caldwell: Conference closed without reaching agreement on
                        quotas.<anchor n="76" xml:id="d512-f1"/> Discussion will be continued in
                    Advisory Committee in January and in the meantime representatives of British,
                    Swiss, German and French Governments are to have further conversations among
                    themselves.</p>
                <p>I am sailing on the <hi rendition="#italic">Leviathan</hi> on the 18th.
                    [Caldwell.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d512-f1" n="76" xml:id="d512-f1-content">
                <p>See League of Nations, <hi rendition="#italic">Traffic in Opium and Other
                        Dangerous Drugs; Conference on the Limitation of the Manufacture of
                        Dangerous Drugs: Report of the Preliminary Meeting of Official
                        Representatives of the Manufacturing Countries, Held in London,
                        October–November 1930</hi> (C.669.M.278.1930.XI).</p>
            </note>
